# The crew: one astronaut per player, one line per ship, in ship order.
# Edit names here and re-run tools/lvc.py; no code changes needed.
#
#   crew <name> ship <ship name> [quirk <quirk from fleet.lv>] [tag <word>]... [flagship]
#        [voice "<short sign-off>"] [habit "<one sentence about {A}>"]
#
# Tags are optional flavour hooks for cards: `when tag A mech` only binds role A to crew
# carrying that tag. Use them to let a card *prefer* someone (pair it with an untagged
# twin), never to lock a whole storyline to one person. Tags never appear in card text.
#
# With no quirk, the astronaut's starting traits are seeded from the voyage key and
# their name, so they are stable from build to build but nobody picked them.
# Card text never assumes anyone's gender: use {A}/{B} or "they".
#
# Voice: one short sign-off in that astronaut's own rhythm, drawn from their habits
# (never invented). Cards print it with {Av}/{Bv}, so a crewmate sounds like
# themselves whatever role the season gives them.
#
# Habits: one small, harmless, real detail per astronaut, sent in by that player and
# dropped in here. It is a whole sentence about {A}, e.g.
#   habit "{A} {A:keeps} one small thing from home within reach of the console."
# Cards marked `each crew` print the first habit (one clone per astronaut, compiled in;
# the phone never sees a new slot). Up to four habits per line: `each habit N` cards
# clone only for astronauts with a real Nth habit, so a quirk line only ever renders
# for its owner. Never invent a habit for a real person: leave it out (or leave the
# placeholder), and no clone is made. To add a ship, add one line here; the
# engine's crew count (lv/state.N, tools/lvc.py N_CREW) must match.

crew Phill     ship Ship 01   tag controls  flagship  voice "Saving here."  habit "{A} {A:keeps} a pot of galley herbs alive under a spare lamp, pinching it back like the beds at home." habit "{A} {A:fixes} a loose locker hinge on the first try, then {A:adds} \"hinges\" to the house to-do list waiting on Earth." habit "Before every burn {A} {A:writes} one line on where everything stands, like a save before a hard level, in case anyone has to load from it."
crew Jacques   ship Ship 02   tag controls  voice "Copy. Done. Next."  habit "{A}'s kit is squared away past any inspection, every strap folded to the same length." habit "{A} still {A:checks} a stock portfolio, on prices minutes old by the time they reach the ship. \"Long position,\" {A} {A:says}, and {A:means} the ship." habit "Every night now {A} {A:lays} the suit out in donning order and {A:runs} the fleet's radio check in ninety crisp seconds." habit "{A} {A:tilts} a spare circuit board to the lamp and {A:reads} it like a letter, a career's habit: the maker's mark, the solder, one rework someone was proud of. Video from home: the chihuahua on patrol, the two cats allowing it."
crew Kim       ship Ship 03   tag controls  voice "And scene."  habit "{A} {A:rations} the episodes queued for the trip, one a week, and the fleet has learned not to call during one." habit "The water processor has a name, a rival and a tragic backstory now, courtesy of {A}, and the ground uses the name in tickets." habit "On each corridor burn {A} {A:allows} the countdown one line of dramatic narration, then {A:flies} it dead straight." habit "Video from home: Mango asleep in {A}'s chair, as ever, and Dirt, the new one, asleep on Mango. {A} {A:narrates} it for the fleet like a nature film."
crew Jai       ship Ship 04   tag controls  voice "Clear. Next mark."  habit "{A} {A:runs} the hatch drill against a stopwatch, calling it short: \"Two, clear. Three, clear. Seal.\" Half a beat ahead of the checklist, never off it." habit "On the flyby plot {A} {A:draws} the trajectory as a racing line, apex marked. The nav team keeps the word." habit "{A} {A:walks} the entry timeline like a qualifying lap: the same marks, called aloud, every night, until the times stop changing." habit "{A} {A:sets} the fantasy football lineup a week early and {A:talks} trash to the league, two minutes late. Dad answers in full JetBlue gate voice, \"We apologise for the delay,\" and saves {A} the first song on the next wedding dance floor."
crew Michelle  ship Ship 05   tag controls  voice "Story first. Numbers next."  habit "{A}'s mail from home carries a kitten count in the subject line, eleven one week, thirteen the next, one always out of frame." habit "{A} {A:keeps} a lint roller in the flight kit, tens of millions of kilometres from any fur, and {A:uses} it before every call home." habit "Near Mars now, word reaches {A}: the last of the spring litter has gone to a home, and the house is briefly, suspiciously quiet." habit "{A} {A:runs} the burn briefing like a Disney queue: a story to keep the line moving. Then the Tesla half takes over: the numbers, to the decimal."
crew Diego     ship Ship 06   tag mech  voice "Now you: how's your day?"  habit "{A} {A:measures} the galley latch twice, {A:finds} it was drawn for a lighter door, and {A:fixes} it with one washer." habit "Mail from whoever is minding {A}'s three cats: all fed, all offended, one asleep in the bag {A} meant to pack." habit "{A} {A:redraws} a sagging locker bracket on a ration wrapper, lighter and stiffer; the ground files it as a drawing." habit "The ground has a new trainee, a stranger for about a minute. {A} {A:opens} with a question; by sign-off, two-minute lag and all, {A} {A:knows} where the trainee grew up, and the trainee knows all three cats by name."
crew Dorian    ship Ship 07   tag controls  voice "Checked. Every line."  habit "The kid at home keeps {A} in drawings: the ship, Mars and a dog, all the same size. {A} {A:keeps} every one." habit "{A} {A:asks} the ship's assistant to summarise the fault log. It answers in one confident paragraph; {A} {A:checks} every line." habit "As Mars fills the cameras, a video: a Boston terrier at the front window, and a small voice telling it {A} {A:is} nearly there." habit "{A} {A:rations} the Uncrustables, one a week, logged like fuel, and {A:sends} the count home so {A:their} kid can cross the week off."
crew Marco     ship Ship 08   tag controls  voice "Capacity: one."  habit "Saturday nights {A} {A:dims} the galley to one light and {A:calls} it the club. Capacity: one. The door policy is strict." habit "{A} {A:finds} the coolant pump cycling in four-four and {A:writes} it a bass line. The ground's acoustic survey comes back marked allegro." habit "A photo reaches {A} from a dark, loud room: friends holding up a sign that says SAVING YOUR SPOT." habit "Before the Saturday club {A} {A:allows} one spray of cologne, a ritual older than the BMW years in Mexico, older than leaving Elgin. In a sealed cabin it lasts all week; the ground's air sample comes back marked \"notes of citrus\"."
